symbolicWeightEDDegree -- symbolically compute ED degrees of affine varieties
*****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        UED = determinantalUnitEDDegree(F)
        GED = determinantalGenericEDDegree(F)
        GED = symbolicWeightEDDegree(F,U,W)
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a system of polynomials (system
        need not be square)
      * U, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a (generic) data vector
      * W, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a (generic) weight vector
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note ReturnCriticalIdeal: ReturnCriticalIdeal, => ..., default value
        false, whether to return the ideal of critical points
  * Outputs:
      * ED, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a generic/unit Euclidean
        distance degree
      * ICP, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, ideal of critical points (if
        ReturnCriticalIdeal is set)

Description
===========

This method computes Euclidean distance (ED) degrees for the variety defined by
the system $F$ via symbolic computation. The ideal of critical points is formed
by saturating the defining ideal of the variety with minors of the Jacobian and
Augmented Jacobian. The degree of this ideal is the ED degree of the variety.
The unit variant of this method computes an ED degree using random (integer)
data and unit weights, whereas the generic variant will use random data and
random weights.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {x^2 + y^2 - 1};                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (U,W) = ({12, 23}, {15, 331});                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : UED = determinantalUnitEDDegree F                                 |
|                                                                       |
|o4 = 2                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : GED = determinantalGenericEDDegree F                              |
|                                                                       |
|o5 = 4                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : ICP = symbolicWeightEDDegree(F, U, W, ReturnCriticalIdeal => true)|
|                                                                       |
|                                    2    2                             |
|o6 = ideal (316x*y - 7613x + 180y, x  + y  - 1)                        |
|                                                                       |
|o6 : Ideal of R                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
* Menu:

* ReturnCriticalIdeal::         whether to return the ideal of critical points

Ways to use symbolicWeightEDDegree:
===================================

  * "symbolicWeightEDDegree(List,List,List)"

