ReturnCriticalIdeal -- whether to return the ideal of critical points
*********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        ICP = symbolicWeightEDDegree(F, U, W, ReturnCriticalIdeal => true)

Description
===========

Symbolic methods compute the Euclidean Distance degree of a variety by
computing the degree of its critical ideal, which defines the critical points
of the distance function on the variety. Setting this option will cause
symbolic methods to return this ideal rather than its degree.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {x^2 + y^2 - 1};                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (U,W) = ({12, 23}, {15, 331});                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : ICP = symbolicWeightEDDegree(F, U, W, ReturnCriticalIdeal => true)|
|                                                                       |
|                                    2    2                             |
|o4 = ideal (316x*y - 7613x + 180y, x  + y  - 1)                        |
|                                                                       |
|o4 : Ideal of R                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

