leftKernelWeightEDDegree -- numerically compute Euclidean distance degrees of complete intersections
****************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        UED = leftKernelUnitEDDegree(F)
        GED = leftKernelGenericEDDegree(F)
        GED = leftKernelWeightEDDegree(F,U,W)
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a system of polynomials (need not
        be square) defining an affine variety that is a complete intersection
      * U, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a (generic) data vector
      * W, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a (generic) weight vector
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note TempDirectory: TempDirectory, => ..., default value null, set
        directory for Bertini runs
  * Outputs:
      * ED, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a generic/unit Euclidean
        distance degree

Description
===========

This method computes Euclidean distance (ED) degrees for affine varieties
defined by the system $F$ numerically using Lagrange multipliers. If the
resulting variety is a complete intersection, the left kernel of the augmented
Jacobian is used to derive a set of critical erquations which are passed into
Bertini. The resulting number of critical points is returned as the ED degree.
The unit variant of this method computes an ED degree using random (complex)
data and unit weights, whereas `leftKernelGenericEDDegree` will use random data
and random weights.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {x^2 + y^2 - 1};                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (U,W) = ({.12, .23}, {.15, .331});                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : UED = leftKernelUnitEDDegree F                                          |
|Warning: The HomVariableGroup is written first and then the AffVariableGroup |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = 2                                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|is written second.                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : GED = leftKernelGenericEDDegree F                                       |
|Warning: The HomVariableGroup is written first and then the AffVariableGroup |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = 4                                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|is written second.                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : GED = leftKernelWeightEDDegree(F, U, W)                                 |
|Warning: The HomVariableGroup is written first and then the AffVariableGroup |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = 4                                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|is written second.                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The computed ED degree may be lower than expected due to path tracking.

* Menu:

* TempDirectory::               set directory for Bertini runs

