File: EuclideanDistanceDegree.info, Node: UseMonodromy, Up: parameterizedWeightEDDegree

UseMonodromy -- whether to use monodromy methods to compute degrees
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        GED = parameterizedWeightEDDegree(F, U, W, UseMonodromy => true)

Description
===========

If this option is set, the parameterized ED degree methods will use the
MonodromySolver to numerically solve the critical equations and report the
number of regular solutions as the ED degree of the parameterized variety.

+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                               |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = {x^2 + 1, x * y, y - 1};                               |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : GED = parameterizedGenericEDDegree(F, UseMonodromy => true)|
|                                                                |
|o3 = 7                                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Using monodromy may result in an ED degree that is less than expected. In
particular, if the parameterization map is $n$-to-one, using monodromy to solve
for the degree may result in a degree than is off by a factor of $n$.

