averageNumericEDDegree -- compute average ED degrees using sampled data
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        aED = averageNumericEDDegree(F, G, 10)
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a system of polynomials (need not
        be square) defining the variety
      * G, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of polynomials (complete
        intersection) such that $V(F)$ is an irreducible component of $V(G)$,
        i.e. a witness model
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, number of samples to take
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Submodel => a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, default value {}, list
        of linear polynomials to slice the variety
      * SampleGenerator => a *note function closure:
        (Macaulay2Doc)FunctionClosure,, default value null, a function which
        generates data samples
      * Tolerance => a *note real number: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,, default value
        .000001, tolerance to use when checking if a critical point is real
      * *note TempDirectory: TempDirectory, => ..., default value null, set
        directory for Bertini runs
  * Outputs:
      * aED, a *note real number: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,, average ED degree after n
        trials

Description
===========

Generate data samples using the given function and uses homotopy continuation
to find critical points of the distance function. The average number of real
critical points after $n$ trials is returned. This method creates a *note
NumericalComputationOptions: NumericalComputationOptions, object and computes
critical points using the *note homotopyEDDegree: homotopyEDDegree, method. By
default, `random(RR)` is used to generate data samples. Points are tested using
the *note realPoints: (NAGtypes)realPoints, function from the *note
NumericalAlgebraicGeometry: (NumericalAlgebraicGeometry)Top, package, a
tolerance can be passed along using the `Tolerance` option, by default it is
1e-6.

+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = G = {x^2 + y^2 - 1};                                            |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : sampleGen = () -> apply(#gens R, i -> random(RR));                  |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : aED = averageNumericEDDegree(F, G, 10, SampleGenerator => sampleGen)|
|                                                                         |
|o4 = 1.9                                                                 |
|                                                                         |
|o4 : RR (of precision 53)                                                |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
* Menu:

* SampleGenerator::

